# BOL improve loop — CONTINUE UNPROMPTED (training)

When this agent (or any concurrent agent) touches Bill of Lading PDF/layout,
**own the improve loop**. Do not stop after one tweak and wait for the user to
re-ask. This loop **trains** BOL layout quality over time (spacing, bleed,
overcrowding, long refs, logo/Probill/Swift clearance).

## Mandatory loop

1. Read `qa_bol/synthetic/improve_summary_latest.json` (create/run the loop
   if missing).
2. Fix the listed **top_failures** / gate fails that are real layout bugs
   (long-field cutoff, logo under Probill/Swift, margin bleed, overcrowding,
   missing orange title bar).
3. Re-run: `python scripts/bol_label_improve_loop.py` from repo root
   (uses `.tools/flutter` + `scripts/bol_label_score.py`).
4. Confirm mean composite and gates move the right way; iterate again if clear
   score-proven bugs remain.
5. Append lessons to `qa_bol/synthetic/training_lessons.json`; expand cases when
   new BOL failure modes appear.

Docs: `qa_bol/synthetic/README.md`. See also `improve-loops-training.mdc`.

## North star

- `filled/qa_bol_preview/bol_preview_latest.png` /
  `mobile/test/generate_bol_preview_test.dart`
- Matrix case `baseline_sample` (`ShippingLabelData.bolSample` + sample logo)

Protect baseline visual quality. Prefer shrink-to-fit / wrap / logo frame
clamping over redesign.

## Hard constraints

- Do **not** change Shipping Label locked SO/Contact constants
  (`afterPillGap` 11.0, under-pill `showRule` false, contact label→value 3.0).
  Do not edit `shipping_label_pdf.dart` locked values as a side effect of BOL work.
- Long Sales Order / PO / Project / Packing List values must remain **visible**
  (shrink or wrap) — never clipped away or empty when the source value is set.
- Customer logos must stay in the left header frame; never invade Probill or
  Swift ink.

## Out of scope for “fixes”

- Do not loosen harness soft gates to hide a regression.
- Do not commit/push unless the user asked. The improve loop itself does not
  require a commit.
